# Wingspan agents → Cursor Subagent

Cursor-ported skills say `Cursor subagent vgv-review-agent`. Dispatch with
Cursor's **Subagent** tool (called Task in older Cursor documentation).

`cursor-link-vgv-skills` materializes each upstream brief as a flat Cursor
plugin agent under `~/.cursor/plugins/local/vgv-*/agents/`, so the VGV names
below are real `subagent_type` values. Cursor only discovers `agents/*.md` one
level deep, which is why the nested upstream tree needs flattening.

Pass the exact VGV `subagent_type` when it appears in the current tool schema.
If it is missing, Cursor has not reloaded the stubs yet — re-run
`./scripts/cursor-link-vgv-skills.sh`, restart Cursor, and only then fall back
to `generalPurpose` with the full brief pasted into `prompt`.

The subagent inherits every parent tool and MCP server but not the
conversation, so its `prompt` must still be self-contained:

- user goal and review scope
- absolute repository and artifact paths
- scope-specific constraints beyond the agent's own brief
- report-writing paths, when the skill expects a raw report
- exact output/report format
- instruction to return only the requested result

Do not rely on `@agent` syntax or merely name the agent in the prompt.

## Tool scoping

Cursor has no per-agent tool allowlist. Subagents inherit the parent's tools,
and the only restriction is `readonly: true` in the agent file, which blocks
file edits and state-changing shell commands. The port sets it on
`flutter-reviewer` (whose upstream `tools:` list named no write tool) and
leaves it off the Wingspan reviewers, which must write raw report files.

`readonly` is an agent-file field, not a Subagent call argument — do not pass
it in the tool call.

## Model pins

Do not pass `model` on the Subagent call unless the user overrides. Each VGV
agent file already pins a Cursor model from the Wingspan tier:

| Upstream | Cursor pin | Intent |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `haiku` | `composer-2.5` | Mechanical / fast (Cursor Models pool) |
| `sonnet` | `claude-sonnet-5` | Deep review / research (Other Models pool) |
| `inherit` | `inherit` | Match the parent (orchestrator reviews) |

Parent chat for brainstorm/plan handoffs should be **Composer 2.5** so
AskQuestion works. See `vgv-cursor-handoff.mdc`.

