## Wingspan dispatch patterns (do these)

### 1. Parallel fan-out (required where skills say so)

When `/build` Phase 3, `/code-review`, `/plan` research, or plan-review
says **in parallel**, launch **multiple Subagent calls in one assistant
turn** (one message, multiple tool uses). Do not serialize them.

| Workflow | Parallel set |
| --- | --- |
| `/plan` local + external research | `codebase-review-agent` + docs/best-practices agents as the skill lists |
| `/plan` / `/plan-technical-review` quality | `code-simplicity-review-agent` + `vgv-review-agent` + `plan-splitting-agent` |
| `/build` Phase 3 | all 5: vgv, architecture, test-quality, simplicity, pr-readiness |
| `/code-review` | vgv, architecture, test-quality, simplicity (+ pr-readiness if shipping) |
| `/hotfix` review | vgv + test-quality (reduced set) |

### 2. Absolute paths + structured raw reports

Before fan-out: `PWD=$(pwd)`. Each review agent prompt must include the
skill's review-agent-instructions (from the ported skill under
`~/.cursor/skills/<skill>/references/`) with:

- `<RAW_DIR>` = absolute path (e.g. `$PWD/docs/reviews/raw`)
- `<name>` = bare stem (`vgv-review`, …)

Agents write `$RAW_DIR/<name>.md` and return the **structured findings
block** only. Parent consolidates per the skill's
`review-consolidation` procedure into one report.

### 3. Non-fatal failures

If one Subagent fails, continue with the others; record the failure in the
consolidated report header. Offer retry for failed agents.

### 4. Parent owns synthesis

Subagents do not edit the plan/PR narrative. Parent merges findings,
applies auto-fixes the skill allows, and presents AskQuestion options.

### 5. AskQuestion for handoffs

After parallel work completes, present skill option lists via
**AskQuestion** (see `vgv-ask-question.mdc`) — never shrink the list.

## Anti-patterns (avoid)

- Sending only an agent name instead of a self-contained specialist prompt
- Guessing a VGV `subagent_type` that is absent from the current tool schema
- Passing `readonly` as a Subagent call argument (it is an agent-file field)
- Falling back to `generalPurpose` before re-running the link script
- Running the 5 `/build` reviewers **sequentially**
- Relative `docs/reviews/...` paths in subagent prompts
- Skipping consolidation and dumping five chat essays
- Copying agent `.md` files into this repo

## Sea Trials extras

Two more `subagent_type` values, shipped by the **sea-trials plugin**:

- `powersync-migration-operator`
- `macos-appstore-signing`

Use those when the work touches PowerSync migrations or App Store
signing — they are not Wingspan agents.

Their sources live in `.cursor/agent-sources/`, not `.cursor/agents/`,
which Cursor would scan as a second registration of the same two names.
Edit there and re-run `--emit-sea-trials-plugin`.

